<div class="head">
  <h1>Publish</h1>
  <div class="head__actions"><a class="btn" href="/site/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Preview site ↗</a></div>
</div>

<div class="note note--info">
  <strong>Two steps, on purpose.</strong>
  <em>Generate</em> rewrites <code>web/</code> from the database — local and repeatable, with no effect on the live site.
  <em>Commit &amp; push</em> is what triggers the DigitalOcean deploy. Keeping them apart means saving a product can never deploy the site by accident.
</div>

<div class="cols">
  <div>
    <div class="panel">
      <div class="panel__head"><h2>1. Generate the site</h2></div>
      <p class="hint">Rewrites every page from the database and runs the SEO checks. A build that fails those checks is reported here and is not safe to push.</p>
      <form method="post" action="/publish/build">
        <button class="btn btn--primary" type="submit">Generate now</button>
      </form>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <div class="panel__head"><h2>2. Commit &amp; push</h2></div>
      <% if (!isRepo) { %>
      <div class="note">
        <strong>Not a git repository yet.</strong> Run these once in the project folder, then reload this page:
        <pre class="log" style="margin-top:.5rem">git init
git add -A
git commit -m "Initial import from Shopify"
git branch -M main
git remote add origin git@github.com:&lt;you&gt;/FlashStore.git
git push -u origin main</pre>
      </div>
      <% } else { %>
      <p class="hint">
        Branch <code><%= branch || '—' %></code>
        <% if (remote) { %>→ <code><%= remote %></code><% } else { %>— <strong>no remote configured</strong>, so a push will fail.<% } %>
      </p>
      <% if (!changes.length) { %>
      <p class="hint">No uncommitted changes. Generate first if you have edited anything.</p>
      <% } else { %>
      <p><strong><%= changes.length %></strong> changed file<%= changes.length === 1 ? '' : 's' %>:</p>
      <pre class="log"><%= changes.slice(0, 40).join('\n') %><%= changes.length > 40 ? '\n… and ' + (changes.length - 40) + ' more' : '' %></pre>
      <% } %>
      <form method="post" action="/publish/push">
        <div class="field" style="max-width:420px">
          <label for="message">Commit message</label>
          <input id="message" name="message" type="text" value="Update catalogue" required>
        </div>
        <div class="field" style="max-width:220px">
          <label for="confirm">Type <code>PUSH</code> to confirm</label>
          <input id="confirm" name="confirm" type="text" autocomplete="off" required>
        </div>
        <button class="btn btn--danger" type="submit"<%= changes.length ? '' : ' disabled' %>>Commit &amp; push (deploys the site)</button>
      </form>
      <% } %>
    </div>

    <% if (output) { %>
    <div class="panel">
      <div class="panel__head"><h2>Log</h2></div>
      <pre class="log"><%= output %></pre>
    </div>
    <% } %>
  </div>

  <div>
    <div class="panel">
      <div class="panel__head"><h2>Recent builds</h2></div>
      <% if (!history.length) { %>
      <p class="hint">No builds recorded yet.</p>
      <% } else { %>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>When (UTC)</th><th class="num">Files</th><th></th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <% history.forEach(function (b) { %>
          <tr>
            <td><%= b.finished_at %></td>
            <td class="num"><%= b.pages_written %></td>
            <td><% if (b.ok) { %><span class="tag tag--ok">ok</span><% } else { %><span class="tag tag--bad">failed</span><% } %></td>
          </tr>
          <% }); %>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <% } %>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <div class="panel__head"><h2>Previewing</h2></div>
      <p class="hint">The <strong>Preview site</strong> link above serves <code>web/</code> through this admin. To check it standalone, exactly as DigitalOcean will serve it, run <code>npm run serve</code> and open <a href="http://localhost:4300/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">localhost:4300</a>.</p>
      <p class="hint">Avoid port 5000 on macOS — Control Center's AirPlay Receiver holds it and returns 403, which looks like a broken site.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <div class="panel__head"><h2>What gets deployed</h2></div>
      <p class="hint">DigitalOcean serves <code>web/</code> exactly as committed — there is no build step in the cloud, so what you generate here is what goes live.</p>
      <p class="hint"><code>data/originals/</code> holds the untouched image archive. It is committed as a backup but sits outside <code>web/</code>, so it is never served to visitors.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
